  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirement\nCompare the maximum number of private repositories allowed in the **Free** and **Pro** plans in GitHub Pricing.\n\n## Screenshot Evidence\n\n**Screenshots 1 & 3 (GitHub Pricing page):** Show the current pricing page with plan cards for Free ($0), Team ($4), and Enterprise ($21). The Free plan card explicitly lists \"Unlimited public/private repositories.\"\n\n**Screenshot 2 (Compare features table):** The pricing page's feature comparison table shows columns only for **Free, Team, and Enterprise** — notably, **Pro is not displayed as a column** on the current pricing page. Under \"Code management,\" the row \"Private repositories\" shows **\"Unlimited\"** for the Free plan (and for Team/Enterprise).\n\n**Screenshots 4 & 5 (GitHub Docs – \"GitHub's plans\"):** Since Pro is absent from the pricing page, the agent consulted GitHub's official documentation:\n- \"GitHub Free for personal accounts\": *\"you can work with unlimited collaborators on unlimited public repositories with a full feature set, and on **unlimited private repositories** with a limited feature set.\"*\n- \"GitHub Pro\" section: *\"In addition to the features available with GitHub Free for personal accounts, GitHub Pro includes...\"* — confirming Pro inherits all Free features (including unlimited private repositories) plus extras like 3,000 Actions minutes and 2 GB Packages storage.\n\n## Assessment of the Response\nThe response accurately reflects the screenshots:\n1. ✅ Correctly identified that the pricing comparison table lists Private repositories as \"Unlimited\" for Free.\n2. ✅ Correctly noted that Pro is no longer a column on the pricing page (visible in Screenshot 2).\n3. ✅ Supplemented with official GitHub Docs to verify Pro includes all Free features, hence unlimited private repositories.\n4. ✅ Delivered the comparison conclusion: **both plans allow unlimited private repositories** — they are equal.\n\nThe task (comparing private repository limits between Free and Pro) was fully accomplished with a correct, well-supported conclusion, including a reasonable workaround for Pro's absence from the pricing table.\n\n## Verdict\n**SUCCESS**",
